{"name":"Freetown","slug":"freetown","region":"Africa","lat":8.48,"lon":-13.23,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Freetown has warmed by about 0.15 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1 °C in all. There is a clear El Niño signal on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 60% of a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 16 years of the long-term trend. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 0.4 °C, against 0.1 °C for the coldest days. Dec–Feb is the dry season in Freetown; rainfall has tended to decline in this record, a trend that station records cannot yet confirm. El Niño has a clear effect toward a drier season with fewer rainy days, and this year's shift is substantial. Humidity shows no clear trend or El Niño link. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 90% chance), about 0.6 °C above the 1991–2020 average, mostly because of the long-term warming trend rather than El Niño; a drier-than-normal season is likely (about 65% chance), partly because of an uncertain long-term drying trend. The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":26.7372,"trend_per_decade":0.1382,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.0368,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0944,"enso_p":0.0371,"confidence":"Clear","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.059,"intrinsic_sd":0.3533,"effect_this_season":0.2177,"effect_ratio":0.6163,"size":"Substantial","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":4,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.5802,"forecast_mean":27.3174,"forecast_sd":0.3816,"p_below":0.027,"p_near":0.0642,"p_above":0.9088,"forecast_words":"Likely (91%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.0861,"shrink_factor":0.9119,"effect_this_season_raw":0.2387,"trend_part_2027":0.3625,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":15.7499,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1882,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0512,"enso_p":0.444,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.1295,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.1294,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0694,"enso_p":0.1257,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.1755,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.1516,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1739,"enso_p":0.0001,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":0.4399,"lines_cross":false},"tails":{"enso_difference":0.1227,"enso_difference_p":0.0648,"trend_difference":-0.0366,"trend_difference_p":0.2389}},"values":[25.94,26.735,26.395,26.25,26.556,26.053,25.519,26.404,26.443,26.603,26.524,26.36,26.696,26.935,25.111,26.601,26.821,25.776,26.351,26.574,26.182,25.999,26.867,26.52,26.13,25.924,25.852,26.457,26.186